---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Experience">
  <h1>Experience</h1>

  <h2>Monkey Strike Games — Technical Lead / Graduate Programmer</h2>
  <p><em>Sep. 2025 – Aug. 2026</em></p>

  <img src="/experience/monkey_strike_games_logo.jpeg" alt="Monkey Strike Games logo" style="width: 50%; height: auto; margin: 1rem 0;" />

  <p>
    Technical Lead at Monkey Strike Games, a startup studio, where my work spans
    the full pipeline: infrastructure (Perforce, Jenkins, VPN) set up on their own servers, rendering
    optimization and baked lighting, and Steam platform integration built
    largely from scratch to cover some custom behavior that was needed (drm and steam input for unreal enhanced input system).
  </p>

  <h3>Pizzapocalypse 2</h3>
  <img src="/experience/Pizzapocalypse2.jpg" alt="Pizzapocalypse 2 thumbnail" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 1rem 0;" />
  <p>
    A UE5.6 production. Set up and maintain the studio's Jenkins CI/CD pipeline
    and Perforce infrastructure, built a Jenkins-triggered automated profiling
    pipeline with input record/replay (deprecated), and implemented PSO precaching/bundling
    to cut down shader-compilation stutter. Also own rendering optimization for
    forward-shaded, densely set-dressed levels — shadow culling, HISM/ISM
    tooling, and baked lighting — plus a custom Steam Input plugin built from
    scratch, drm and general build compiling and packaging errors/bugs fixing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4021890/Pizzapocalypse_2/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on Steam →</a>
  </p>
  <video controls style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    <source src="/experience/Pizzapocalypse2.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    Your browser does not support the video tag.
  </video>

  <h3>DrinkUpCowboy</h3>
  <img src="/experience/DrinkUpCowboy.jpg" alt="DrinkUpCowboy thumbnail" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 1rem 0;" />
  <p>
    Working on multiplayer and replication systems for this second title on
    the same studio infrastructure — an area I'm actively building depth in.
    Session establishment runs through Steam's networking as the
    third-party layer, with peer-to-peer connections rather than a
    dedicated server model.
    This was done in order to build a prototype for a possible gameplay loop for publishers so the end result might not end up in the final build.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/3861080/Drink_Up_Cowboy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on Steam →</a>
  </p>
  <video controls style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    <source src="/experience/DrinkUpCowboy.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    Your browser does not support the video tag.
  </video>
</Layout>